From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: never hand the SDIO DMA a fragment shorter than its
 alignment bounce

0013 gives every page fragment of a frame to the SDIO host as its own
scatterlist entry. The SDHCI ADMA (sdhci_adma_table_pre) copies a
buffer's first bytes up to 4-byte alignment into a bounce area and
describes the rest as one transfer. A fragment shorter than those first
bytes, 1 to 3 bytes at an unaligned address, leaves a negative length,
stored as 0xFFFF or 0xFFFE: the controller then reads the kernel memory
after the fragment into the card's FIFO in place of the rest of the
aggregate. TCP cuts such pieces at small receive windows or segment
boundaries; a peer advertising a 1-3 byte window forces them.

- aicwf_adma_add() linearizes a frame with a fragment shorter than 4
  bytes before laying it out.
- aicwf_sdio_write_sg() refuses such an entry as a backstop.

The header entry (at least the 4-byte SDIO header) and the zeroed fill
buffer (kzalloc) are never that short and unaligned.
---
diff --git a/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c b/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
index ec55317..95f3d19 100644
--- a/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
+++ b/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
@@ -1547,6 +1547,9 @@ static int aicwf_sdio_write_sg(struct sdio_func *func, unsigned int addr,
 	for (i = 0; i < nents; i++) {
 		if (!list[i].len)
 			continue;
+		/* Never a buffer shorter than its alignment bounce (aicwf_adma_add). */
+		if (list[i].len < ((4 - ((uintptr_t)list[i].buf & 3)) & 3))
+			return -EINVAL;
 		sg_set_buf(&sg[n++], list[i].buf, list[i].len);
 		sum += list[i].len;
 	}
@@ -1626,6 +1629,19 @@ int aicwf_adma_add(struct aicwf_tx_priv *tx_priv, struct sk_buff *pkt)
 	 * as linearizing moves the head. */
 	if (skb_has_frag_list(pkt) && skb_linearize(pkt))
 		return -ENOMEM;
+	/* The SDHCI ADMA copies a buffer's first bytes up to 4-byte alignment
+	 * into a bounce area and gives the controller the rest as one
+	 * descriptor. A fragment shorter than those first bytes (TCP cuts 1 to
+	 * 3 byte pieces at small windows) leaves a negative length, written as
+	 * about 64 KiB: the controller would read the memory after it. Such a
+	 * frame goes linear. */
+	for (f = 0; f < skb_shinfo(pkt)->nr_frags; f++) {
+		if (skb_frag_size(&skb_shinfo(pkt)->frags[f]) < TX_ALIGNMENT) {
+			if (skb_linearize(pkt))
+				return -ENOMEM;
+			break;
+		}
+	}
 	entries = 1 + skb_shinfo(pkt)->nr_frags + (pad ? 1 : 0);
 	if (tx_priv->aggr_segcnt + entries + 1 > tx_priv->max_segs && atomic_read(&tx_priv->aggr_count) > 0) {
 		tx_priv->fw_avail_bufcnt -= atomic_read(&tx_priv->aggr_count);
